      {
        "id": 127636,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-15T02:17:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"HappiestMeal\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/22d042/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> HappiestMeal:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Perhaps this was answered before but I couldnt find it with a search. &nbsp;If you are dealt 0 damage are you considered to have take. Damage for game effects? &nbsp;&nbsp;Example if wraith has combat stance (the first time you are dealt damage a turn deal the source of that damage 2 miles damage) out and sky scraper uses her huge power reall all non hero targets 2 sonic and all hero targets 0 sonic damage). Does combat stance activate dealing 2 damage to sky scraper?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>combat stance would not activate unless you were actually dealt one or more damage. &nbsp;If the final result is zero damage then combat stance would not activate. &nbsp;</p>\n<blockquote></blockquote>\n<p>because I had capt cosmic with his construct that lets him use powers when dealt damage and I was using powers all over the place. &nbsp;Was that legal?</p>\n<p>For the constructs that require damage to activate they need to be dealt at least one damage and still be in play after the damage is dealt. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Edit: dang ninjaed by Pydro</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:02:16.623Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
